# --- influxdb/pgvector: third-party data-bearing images, pulled as `image:` (not built from a
#     Dockerfile we own). influxdb was bumped 2.8.0 -> 2.9.1 (same-major OSS 2.x point release,
#     the newest available) on round 2 of TAP-6622: it cleared several previously-ignored
#     Go-stdlib/openssl/libssl3 CVEs outright (removed below as stale) but did NOT clear the
#     remaining Go-module CVEs baked into influxdb's compiled binaries (golang.org/x/crypto,
#     google.golang.org/grpc, stdlib, etc.) -- those have a FixedVersion per Trivy (the Go
#     ecosystem has patched versions) but the fix is only actionable if InfluxData recompiles
#     and republishes the binary; a further major upgrade (InfluxDB 3.x) is a data-migration
#     project out of scope for TAP-6622. Per the audit's own predicate those ids may NOT be
#     ignored merely because we can't act on them ourselves, so they were removed from this file
#     instead -- scan-all is expected to be red on influxdb/pgvector for those ids until a fixed
#     upstream image ships. See PR body: needs-decision: influxdb major upgrade.
#     pgvector/pgvector:pg17 is already the newest pg17-compatible build on Docker Hub (no
#     newer same-major tag exists); its remaining ignored ids below are genuinely FixedVersion-empty.
CVE-2026-86140 # libxml2 (pgvector/pgvector:pg17, bookworm): no distro fix yet; also a data-bearing third-party image
